    "text": "# Engineering Handbook: Incident Response for AquaCore Control Systems (ACCS)\n\n**Document ID:** ACCS-IR-2024-01\n**Version:** 3.2\n**Classification:** Internal Engineering / Critical Infrastructure\n**Applicability:** All AquaCore Control Service (ACS) Field Engineers, SCADA Architects, and NOC (Network Operations Center) Staff.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction and Scope\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\nThis handbook defines the standardized procedures for detecting, analyzing, containing, and recovering from incidents affecting the AquaCore Control Service (ACCS). ACCS is a distributed SCADA (Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition) and IoT platform used to monitor and control municipal water treatment plants, pumping stations, and distribution networks.\n\n### 1.2 Criticality Levels\nIncidents are classified based on impact to public health, environmental safety, and operational continuity.\n\n| Level | Designation | Definition | Response Time |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P1** | **Critical** | Immediate threat to public health (e.g., chlorine dosing failure, backflow prevention failure) or total loss of control over a major facility. |",
